REFERENCE ONLY -- NOT built, applied, or shipped by this repo. Out-of-tree
kernel (amdgpu/amdkfd) driver source, not a userspace ROCm component this
repo's Docker image build touches. Per AGENTS.md's standing rule, driver
changes belong outside this repo -- this file exists purely as documentation
for a real, hardware-verified kernel bug found and fixed while chasing a
severe vLLM engine-startup hang. See vllm-gfx803/NOTES.md for the full
investigation.

WHY: a thread could block forever inside
rocr::core::InterruptSignal::WaitRelaxed() (via
BlitKernel::SubmitLinearCopyCommand -> RegionMemory::Freeze() ->
ExecutableImpl::Freeze(), i.e. every compiled-kernel-binary "load into GPU"
operation) with zero dmesg activity and zero GPU ring timeout -- the GPU had
genuinely finished the copy, but the completion wakeup never reached the
waiting userspace thread. Confirmed via live native gdb backtraces (17+
minutes parked in this exact call) and full unfiltered `dmesg -T` showing no
corroborating driver-level event on any ring/watchdog.

Root cause: kfd_events.c's kfd_signal_event_interrupt() ->
lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id() has a fast path that, for interrupt
sources with a wide-enough id bit-width (bits > 31, always true for
gfx7/8's 28-bit context_id), calls idr_find(&p->event_idr, id) directly --
trusting the interrupt payload's context_id as an exact event ID -- unless
signal_mailbox_updated is true AND the event's signal-page slot reads as
UNSIGNALED_EVENT_SLOT, in which case it correctly returns NULL and falls
through to the caller's safe exhaustive-scan fallback.

The bug: cik_event_interrupt.c (gfx7/8's own interrupt handler) hardcodes
signal_mailbox_updated=true for CIK_INTSRC_CP_END_OF_PIPE and
CIK_INTSRC_SDMA_TRAP interrupts, even though this hardware generation has no
real firmware mailbox-confirmation mechanism -- the function's own upstream
comment documents gfx7/8's context_id/event IDs as unreliable ("old ASICs
that don't have the event ID or event IDs are incorrect in the IH
payload"). Trusting a coincidentally-signaled-looking slot for a possibly-
garbage context_id means the fast path can silently drop the real target
event's completion interrupt (permanent missed wakeup -- the waiter hangs
forever) or wake an unrelated event that happens to share the same numeric
slot, all without ever reaching the safe scan.

This traces to upstream commit de844846f72b152119faaef1b363448dc8ea368f
("drm/amdkfd: Improve signal event slow path", Philip Yang, 2024-12-19),
which introduced this fast-path shape as a `goto out_unlock` early exit;
kernel 7.1.9's source has since refactored the same logic into
lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id(), but the underlying trust-the-ID-
without-real-confirmation flaw persists unchanged. An independently-filed
freedesktop.org/amd-gfx regression report ("[REGRESSION] RX-580 (gfx803)
GPU hangs since ~v6.14.1") bisected the same symptom to this same commit.
AMD has explicitly declined to investigate gfx803/RX580 issues on kernels
above 6.11 (EOL card, unsupported) -- see ROCm/ROCm#4965.

WHAT: in lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id(), bail to the safe fallback
whenever signal_mailbox_updated is false (previously only checked the
UNSIGNALED_EVENT_SLOT case); in cik_event_interrupt.c, pass
signal_mailbox_updated=false for all three kfd_signal_event_interrupt()
call sites in cik_event_interrupt_wq() (was hardcoded true), accurately
reflecting that gfx7/8 has no real mailbox confirmation.

Applies to: drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_events.c (function
lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id()) and
drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/cik_event_interrupt.c (function
cik_event_interrupt_wq()), against Fedora's kernel-7.1.9-200.fc44 source.
Built as a standalone out-of-tree amdgpu.ko module against the box's
running 7.1.8-200.fc44 headers (same recipe as this repo's other
REFERENCE- kernel patches; the aggregate Fedora/RHEL patch between 7.1.8
and 7.1.9 touches zero files under drivers/gpu/drm/amd), installed over the
stock module, rebooted. Confirmed fixed: the hang that previously
reproduced on ~10 separate attempts over several hours did not recur across
repeated vLLM engine-startup runs after installing this build; engine init
dropped from 60-90+ minutes (or indefinite hangs) to ~22 seconds.

Worth reporting upstream to gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues (the
freedesktop.org thread referenced above already has the bisection; this
patch is a candidate fix, not yet submitted).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_events.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_events.c
@@ -748,10 +748,20 @@ static struct kfd_event *lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id(
 	struct kfd_event *ev;

 	if (id >= KFD_SIGNAL_EVENT_LIMIT)
 		return NULL;

 	if (bits > 31 || (1U << bits) >= KFD_SIGNAL_EVENT_LIMIT) {
+		/* Without a firmware-confirmed mailbox update, the ID is not
+		 * trustworthy on hardware whose IH payload event ID is known
+		 * to be unreliable (gfx7/8 -- see cik_event_interrupt.c, which
+		 * passes signal_mailbox_updated=false for exactly this reason).
+		 * Fall back to the caller's exhaustive scan instead of risking
+		 * a lookup against a garbage ID: that can either silently drop
+		 * the real signaled event (permanent missed wakeup, hangs the
+		 * waiter forever) or wake an unrelated event that happens to
+		 * share the same numeric slot.
+		 */
+		if (!signal_mailbox_updated)
+			return NULL;
+
 		if (signal_mailbox_updated &&
 		    page_slots(p->signal_page)[id] == UNSIGNALED_EVENT_SLOT)
 			return NULL;

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/cik_event_interrupt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/cik_event_interrupt.c
@@ -.. cik_event_interrupt_wq() ..@@
+	/* signal_mailbox_updated=false: gfx7/8's IH payload event ID is not
+	 * reliable (this is the hardware class the exhaustive-scan slow path
+	 * in kfd_signal_event_interrupt/lookup_signaled_event_by_partial_id
+	 * exists for). Trusting it directly here intermittently drops the
+	 * real completion event or wakes the wrong one -- root-caused via a
+	 * hung SubmitLinearCopyCommand/InterruptSignal::WaitRelaxed wait that
+	 * never returned despite the GPU having completed the copy.
+	 */
 	if (ihre->source_id == CIK_INTSRC_CP_END_OF_PIPE)
-		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id, 28, true);
+		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id, 28, false);
 	else if (ihre->source_id == CIK_INTSRC_SDMA_TRAP)
-		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id, 28, true);
+		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id, 28, false);
 	else if (ihre->source_id == CIK_INTSRC_SQ_INTERRUPT_MSG)
-		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id & 0xff, 8, true);
+		kfd_signal_event_interrupt(pasid, context_id & 0xff, 8, false);
